        "hadith-eng":"\"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! We expect to meet the enemy tomorrow and we have no knives.' So the Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'As long as it causes blood to flow, and Allah's Name has been mentioned over it, then eat it, provided that it was not done with a tooth or nail. And I will tell you why: As for the tooth it is a bone, and as for the nail it is the knife of the Ethiopians.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1491, Book 18, Hadith 33",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"Why is it important to mention Allah's Name when slaughtering an animal?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"We were with the Prophet (ﷺ) on journey when the camel that belonged to some people ran away and they did not have a horse. So a man shot it with an arrow and Allah stopped it. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Of these beasts there are some that are as wild as wild animals. So if one of them does this, then treat it similarly.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1492, Book 18, Hadith 35",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How did the Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) suggest dealing with runaway animals?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"A human does no action from the actions on the day of Nahr more beloved to Allah then spilling blood (of sacrificial animals). On the Day of Judgement, it will appear with its horns, and hair, and hooves, and indeed the blood will be accepted by Allah from where it is received before it even falls upon earth, so let your heart delight in it.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1493, Book 19, Hadith 1",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How does the act of sacrificing animals on the day of Nahr relate to the Day of Judgement?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slaughtered two horned male sheep which were mostly white. He slaughtered them with his hand and mentioned Allah's Name, and he said 'Allahu Akbar', and put his foot on their side.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1494, Book 19, Hadith 2",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"Why is it important to say 'Allahu Akbar' during the process of slaughtering an animal?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That 'Ali used to slaughter two male sheep, one for the Prophet (ﷺ) and the other for himself. When this was mentioned to him, he said: \"He ordered me to\" - meaning the Prophet (ﷺ) - \"So I will never leave it.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1495, Book 19, Hadith 3",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"Why might someone continue a practice that was specifically instructed by the Prophet (ﷺ)?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slaughtered a horned male ram of fine pedigree, (around) his mouth was black, and his legs were black, and (around) his eyes was black.",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1496, Book 19, Hadith 4",
        "grade":"Hasan(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"What significance does the description of the ram hold in Islamic traditions?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"A Marfu' narration (from the Prophet (ﷺ)), saying: \"A crippled animal whose limp is obvious is not to be slaughtered as sacrifice, nor an animal with a bad eye whose blindness is obvious, nor a sick animal whose sickness is obvious, nor an emaciated animal that has no marrow (in its bones).\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1497, Book 19, Hadith 5",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"Why is it important for the animal to be healthy and free from defects for sacrifice?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered that we check the eyes and ears, and not to slaughter the Muqabalah, nor the Mudabarah, nor the Sharqa', nor the Kharqa'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1498, Book 19, Hadith 7",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"Why is it important to check the eyes and ears of animals before slaughtering them?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"I brought a Jadha' sheep to Al-Madinah (for sale) but it remained with me. I saw Abu Hurairah and I asked him about it, so he said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: \"The best male\" - or - \"female Udhiyah is that from the Jadha' sheep.\" He said: \"So the people took note of that (they became interested in buying).\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1499, Book 19, Hadith 9",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How did the Prophet Muhammad's (ﷺ) sayings influence the market and people's buying behavior?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave him sheep to distribute among his Companions as a sacrifice. \"There remained a young male kid or a young billy goat, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said: 'Sacrifice it for yourself.'\"\nWaki' said: \"The Jadha' among sheep is seven or six months.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1500, Book 19, Hadith 10",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How does one determine the eligibility of an animal for sacrifice in Islam?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a journey when the (Day of) Adha came, so we shared seven for a cow and ten for a camel.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1501, Book 19, Hadith 12",
        "grade":"Hasan(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How many people can share in the sacrifice of a cow during Eid al-Adha?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"We performed the Nahr (sacrifice) with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at Al-Hudaibiyyah: A camel for seven (persons) and a cow for seven (persons).\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1502, Book 19, Hadith 13",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How many people can share in the sacrifice of a camel according to Islamic tradition?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"Ali said: 'A cow is for seven.' I said: \"And if it gives birth?' He said: 'Then slaughter its offspring with it.' I said: 'What if it is lame?' He said: 'When it has reached the place of ritual.' I said: 'What if it has a broken horn?' He said: 'There is no harm, we were ordered' - or - 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered us, to check the two eyes and the two ears.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1503, Book 19, Hadith 14",
        "grade":"Hasan(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"What should be done if a sacrificial animal gives birth before the sacrifice?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited that an animal with a A'dab (stump) horn or ear should be slaughtered as a sacrifice.\" Qatadah (one of the narrators) said: \"So I mentioned this to Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab and he said: 'The A'dab is that which equals or more than that.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1504, Book 19, Hadith 15",
        "grade":"Hasan(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"Why is it important to follow specific guidelines when selecting animals for sacrifice?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"I asked Abu Abyub [Al-Ansari] how the slaughtering was done during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: 'A man would sacrifice a sheep for himself and the people in his household. They would eat from it and feed others, until the people (later) would boast about it and it became as you see now.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1505, Book 19, Hadith 16",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"What changes occurred in the practice of animal sacrifice over time according to historical accounts?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That a man asked Ibn 'Umar about the Udhiyah, \"Is it obligatory?\" So he said: \"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed the Udhiyah as did the Muslims.\" He repeated the question. So he said: \"Do you understand ?\" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slaughtered as did the Muslims.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1506, Book 19, Hadith 17",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How did the Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) and the early Muslims practice Udhiyah?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stayed in Al-Madinah for ten years performing the Udhiyah.",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1507, Book 19, Hadith 18",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"What is the significance of performing Udhiyah in Islam?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a sermon to us on the Day of Nahr and he said: 'None of you should slaughter until he performs the Salat.\" He said: 'So my maternal uncle stood and said: ' O Messenger of Allah, this is the day in which meat is disliked, and I hastened my sacrifice to feed my family and the people of my dwellings - or - 'my neighbors.' He said: 'Repeat your slaughter with another.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) I have a she-kid that has better meat than my sheep, should I slaughter it?' He said: 'Yes, and it is better and it will suffice for you, but a Jadha' will not be accepted after you.' \"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1508, Book 19, Hadith 19",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How does the hadith address the issue of feeding one's family and neighbors during Eid al-Adha?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"None of you should eat from the meat of his sacrificial animal beyond three days.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1509, Book 19, Hadith 20",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How does the practice of distributing sacrificial meat reflect on community welfare and sharing?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"From his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"I used to prohibit you from (eating) the meat of Sacrifice beyond three days so that those who have the ability would give to those who do not have it. So (now) eat  as you like, feed others, and save from it.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1510, Book 19, Hadith 21",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How does the guidance on consuming sacrificial meat change over time according to the Prophet's instructions?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"I said to the Mother of the Believers: 'Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibit from the meat of the sacrifice?' She said: 'No, but only a few people could slaughter, so he liked that they feed those who did not slaughter. (Later) we would store a leg to eat after ten days.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1511, Book 19, Hadith 22",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How did the scarcity of resources influence the practices related to sacrificial meat during the Prophet's time?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"There is no Fara' or 'Atirah.\"\nThe Fara' is the first of the offspring that would be born to them, so they would slaughter it.\nThe 'Atirah was an animal that they would slaughter during Rajab to honor the month of Rajab, since it was the first of the sacred months.",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1512, Book 19, Hadith 23",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"What is the significance of the month of Rajab in pre-Islamic traditions?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"They entered upon Hafsah bint 'Abdur-Rahman to ask her about the 'Aqiqah. She informed them that 'Aishah had informed her, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered them that for a boy, two sheep were sufficient, and for a girl one sheep.",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1513, Book 19, Hadith 24",
        "grade":"Hasan(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How many sheep are recommended for the 'Aqiqah of a boy?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That his father said: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say the Adhan in the ear of Al-Hasan bin 'Ali - when he was born to Fatimah - the Adhan of Salat.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1514, Book 19, Hadith 25",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How does the practice of saying the Adhan relate to the birth of a child in Islam?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"For a boy, there is an 'Aqiqah. So spill blood for him and remove the harm from him.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1515, Book 19, Hadith 26",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"What actions are recommended to be performed during the 'Aqiqah ceremony?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That she asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the 'Aqiqah. He said: \"For the boy is two sheep, and for the girl is one, it will not harm you if they (i.e. the sheep) are male or female.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1516, Book 19, Hadith 28",
        "grade":"",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How many sheep are recommended for 'Aqiqah for a newborn boy and girl?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"The best of Udhiyah (sacrifice) is a ram, and the best (burial) shroud is the Hullah.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1517, Book 19, Hadith 29",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"What is the significance of choosing a ram for Udhiyah in Islam?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"We were standing with the Prophet (ﷺ) at 'Arafat when I heard him say: 'O you people! For every household each year is Udhiyah (sacrifice) and 'Atirah. Do you know what an 'Atirah is ? It is that which you call Ar-Rajabiyyah.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1518, Book 19, Hadith 30",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"What is the practice of 'Atirah and how is it related to the month of Rajab?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That Ali bin Abi Talib said: \"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had the 'Aqiqah for Al-Hasan with one sheep, and said: 'O Fatimah! Shave his head and give the weight of his hair in silver as charity.'\" He said: \"So I weighed it, and it was the weight of a Dirham or a bit of a Dirham.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1519, Book 19, Hadith 31",
        "grade":"Hasan(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"What is the recommended practice regarding the newborn's hair in Islamic tradition?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"From his father, that the Prophet (ﷺ) gave a Khutbah, then he descended and called for two rams and slaughtered them.",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1520, Book 19, Hadith 32",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"What is the importance of slaughtering rams in Islamic tradition?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"I attended the Eid Al-Adha' with the Prophet (ﷺ) at the Musalla. When he finished his Khutbah, he descended from his Minbar and was given a male sheep. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slaughtered it with his hand and said: 'Bismillah, Wa Allahu Akbar, this from me and whoever does not slaughter from my Ummah.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1521, Book 19, Hadith 33",
        "grade":"Hasan(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"What is the role of the Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) in performing sacrifices on behalf of his Ummah?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"The boy is mortgaged by his 'Aqiqah; slaughtering should be done for him on the seventh day, he should be given a name, and his head should be shaved.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1522, Book 19, Hadith 34",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"On which day should the 'Aqiqah be performed for a newborn according to Islamic tradition?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever sees the crescent of Dhul-Hijjah, and wants to slaughter a sacrifice he should not take from his hair nor from his nails.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1523, Book 19, Hadith 36",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"What is the significance of refraining from cutting hair and nails before offering a sacrifice?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"There is no vowing for disobedience, and its atonement is the atonement of an oath.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1524, Book 20, Hadith 1",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How should one atone for a vow that involves disobedience?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"There is no vowing in disobedience to Allah, and its atonement is the atonement of an oath.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1525, Book 20, Hadith 2",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"What is the prescribed atonement for breaking an oath in Islam?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever vowed to obey Allah, then he should obey Him. And whoever vowed to disobey Allah, then he should not disobey Him.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1526, Book 20, Hadith 3",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How should a person act if they have vowed to do something that is considered disobedient to Allah?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"It is not for a person to vow about that over which he has no control.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1527, Book 20, Hadith 5",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"Why is it important to have control over what one vows?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"The atonement of a vow when it is not specified is the atonement of an oath.\"",
