        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1540, Book 20, Hadith 19",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"Why might the Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) use an oath involving the 'Changer of the Hearts'?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Whoever frees a believing slave, then Allah frees a limb from the Fire for each of his limbs, such that he frees his private parts in lieu of his private parts.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1541, Book 20, Hadith 20",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #2",
        "question":"How does freeing a slave relate to one's salvation from the Fire in Islamic teachings?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"We were seven brothers without a servant except one, and one of us slapped her, so the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered us to free her.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1542, Book 20, Hadith 21",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
