        "grade":"Hasan(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How many people can share in the sacrifice of a camel during Eid al-Adha?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"We performed the Nahr (sacrifice) with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at Al-Hudaibiyyah: A camel for seven (persons) and a cow for seven (persons).\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1502, Book 19, Hadith 13",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How many people can share in the sacrifice of a cow according to Islamic tradition?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"Ali said: 'A cow is for seven.' I said: \"And if it gives birth?' He said: 'Then slaughter its offspring with it.' I said: 'What if it is lame?' He said: 'When it has reached the place of ritual.' I said: 'What if it has a broken horn?' He said: 'There is no harm, we were ordered' - or - 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered us, to check the two eyes and the two ears.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1503, Book 19, Hadith 14",
        "grade":"Hasan(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How should one handle a sacrificial animal that is lame or has a broken horn?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited that an animal with a A'dab (stump) horn or ear should be slaughtered as a sacrifice.\" Qatadah (one of the narrators) said: \"So I mentioned this to Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab and he said: 'The A'dab is that which equals or more than that.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1504, Book 19, Hadith 15",
        "grade":"Hasan(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How does the condition of an animal's physical features affect its eligibility for sacrifice?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"I asked Abu Abyub [Al-Ansari] how the slaughtering was done during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: 'A man would sacrifice a sheep for himself and the people in his household. They would eat from it and feed others, until the people (later) would boast about it and it became as you see now.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1505, Book 19, Hadith 16",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What was the communal aspect of animal sacrifice in early Islamic society?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That a man asked Ibn 'Umar about the Udhiyah, \"Is it obligatory?\" So he said: \"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed the Udhiyah as did the Muslims.\" He repeated the question. So he said: \"Do you understand ?\" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slaughtered as did the Muslims.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1506, Book 19, Hadith 17",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What can be inferred about the obligation of Udhiyah from the actions of the Prophet (ﷺ)?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stayed in Al-Madinah for ten years performing the Udhiyah.",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1507, Book 19, Hadith 18",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What can be learned from the Prophet's practice of performing Udhiyah for ten years in Al-Madinah?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) delivered a sermon to us on the Day of Nahr and he said: 'None of you should slaughter until he performs the Salat.\" He said: 'So my maternal uncle stood and said: ' O Messenger of Allah, this is the day in which meat is disliked, and I hastened my sacrifice to feed my family and the people of my dwellings - or - 'my neighbors.' He said: 'Repeat your slaughter with another.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) I have a she-kid that has better meat than my sheep, should I slaughter it?' He said: 'Yes, and it is better and it will suffice for you, but a Jadha' will not be accepted after you.' \"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1508, Book 19, Hadith 19",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What guidance does the hadith provide regarding the type of animal that can be sacrificed?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"None of you should eat from the meat of his sacrificial animal beyond three days.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1509, Book 19, Hadith 20",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What are the guidelines for handling and distributing sacrificial meat in Islam?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"From his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"I used to prohibit you from (eating) the meat of Sacrifice beyond three days so that those who have the ability would give to those who do not have it. So (now) eat  as you like, feed others, and save from it.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1510, Book 19, Hadith 21",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What are the recommended actions regarding the distribution and consumption of sacrificial meat?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"I said to the Mother of the Believers: 'Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibit from the meat of the sacrifice?' She said: 'No, but only a few people could slaughter, so he liked that they feed those who did not slaughter. (Later) we would store a leg to eat after ten days.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1511, Book 19, Hadith 22",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What is the significance of storing sacrificial meat for later consumption in Islamic tradition?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"There is no Fara' or 'Atirah.\"\nThe Fara' is the first of the offspring that would be born to them, so they would slaughter it.\nThe 'Atirah was an animal that they would slaughter during Rajab to honor the month of Rajab, since it was the first of the sacred months.",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1512, Book 19, Hadith 23",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How did the Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) address the customs of Fara' and 'Atirah?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"They entered upon Hafsah bint 'Abdur-Rahman to ask her about the 'Aqiqah. She informed them that 'Aishah had informed her, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered them that for a boy, two sheep were sufficient, and for a girl one sheep.",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1513, Book 19, Hadith 24",
        "grade":"Hasan(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What is the prescribed number of sheep for the 'Aqiqah of a girl?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That his father said: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say the Adhan in the ear of Al-Hasan bin 'Ali - when he was born to Fatimah - the Adhan of Salat.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1514, Book 19, Hadith 25",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What is the role of the Adhan in welcoming a newborn into the Muslim community?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"For a boy, there is an 'Aqiqah. So spill blood for him and remove the harm from him.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1515, Book 19, Hadith 26",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How does the practice of 'Aqiqah relate to the concept of removing harm?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That she asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the 'Aqiqah. He said: \"For the boy is two sheep, and for the girl is one, it will not harm you if they (i.e. the sheep) are male or female.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1516, Book 19, Hadith 28",
        "grade":"",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"Does the gender of the sheep matter in the practice of 'Aqiqah?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"The best of Udhiyah (sacrifice) is a ram, and the best (burial) shroud is the Hullah.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1517, Book 19, Hadith 29",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What is regarded as the best material for a burial shroud in Islamic teachings?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"We were standing with the Prophet (ﷺ) at 'Arafat when I heard him say: 'O you people! For every household each year is Udhiyah (sacrifice) and 'Atirah. Do you know what an 'Atirah is ? It is that which you call Ar-Rajabiyyah.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1518, Book 19, Hadith 30",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How often is the sacrifice of Udhiyah required for each household?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That Ali bin Abi Talib said: \"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had the 'Aqiqah for Al-Hasan with one sheep, and said: 'O Fatimah! Shave his head and give the weight of his hair in silver as charity.'\" He said: \"So I weighed it, and it was the weight of a Dirham or a bit of a Dirham.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1519, Book 19, Hadith 31",
        "grade":"Hasan(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How is charity related to the practice of 'Aqiqah?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"From his father, that the Prophet (ﷺ) gave a Khutbah, then he descended and called for two rams and slaughtered them.",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1520, Book 19, Hadith 32",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How does the act of slaughtering animals relate to religious practices in Islam?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"I attended the Eid Al-Adha' with the Prophet (ﷺ) at the Musalla. When he finished his Khutbah, he descended from his Minbar and was given a male sheep. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slaughtered it with his hand and said: 'Bismillah, Wa Allahu Akbar, this from me and whoever does not slaughter from my Ummah.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1521, Book 19, Hadith 33",
        "grade":"Hasan(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What is the importance of attending the Eid prayer at the Musalla according to Islamic tradition?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"The boy is mortgaged by his 'Aqiqah; slaughtering should be done for him on the seventh day, he should be given a name, and his head should be shaved.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1522, Book 19, Hadith 34",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What are the recommended practices for a newborn on the seventh day after birth in Islam?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever sees the crescent of Dhul-Hijjah, and wants to slaughter a sacrifice he should not take from his hair nor from his nails.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1523, Book 19, Hadith 36",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How does the sighting of the crescent of Dhul-Hijjah relate to the rituals of sacrifice?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"There is no vowing for disobedience, and its atonement is the atonement of an oath.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1524, Book 20, Hadith 1",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What is the relationship between vows and oaths in Islamic teachings?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"There is no vowing in disobedience to Allah, and its atonement is the atonement of an oath.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1525, Book 20, Hadith 2",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How does Islam view vows that contradict religious obligations?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever vowed to obey Allah, then he should obey Him. And whoever vowed to disobey Allah, then he should not disobey Him.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1526, Book 20, Hadith 3",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What are the consequences of making a vow to disobey Allah?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"It is not for a person to vow about that over which he has no control.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1527, Book 20, Hadith 5",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What are the consequences of making vows about matters beyond one's control?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"The atonement of a vow when it is not specified is the atonement of an oath.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1528, Book 20, Hadith 6",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What is the relationship between vows and oaths in Islamic teachings?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"O 'Abdur-Rahman! Do not ask for a position of leadership, for if you receive it due to asking, you will be left alone with it, and if you receive it without asking, then you will be aided in it. And if you take an oath and you see that something else is better than it, then do what is better, and make an atonement for your oath.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1529, Book 20, Hadith 7",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How should one act if they find a better option after taking an oath?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever takes an oath, and then he sees that something else is better than it, then he should make atonement for his oath and then do it.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1530, Book 20, Hadith 8",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How does Islam view the concept of changing one's decision if a better option is found?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever swears about an oath and says: 'If Allah wills (Insha Allah), then there is no breaking of the oath against him.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1531, Book 20, Hadith 9",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What are the implications of breaking an oath when 'Insha Allah' is included?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever swears [about an oath] and says: 'If Allah wills (Insha Allah), then he will not have broken it.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1532, Book 20, Hadith 10",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What are the implications of breaking an oath in Islam?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"From his father (Ibn 'Umar) that the Prophet (ﷺ) heard 'Umar saying: \"By my father, By my father!\" So he said: \"Verily Allah prohibits you from swearing by your father.\" So 'Umar said: \"By Allah I did not swear by him after that, neither intentionally nor in narrating.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1533, Book 20, Hadith 11",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What was Umar's response to the Prophet's (ﷺ) prohibition on swearing by one's father?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came across 'Umar while he was on his mount, and he was swearing by his father. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Verily Allah prohibits you from swearing by your fathers. So let the one who swears, swear by Allah, or be silent.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1534, Book 20, Hadith 12",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What are the consequences of swearing by one's ancestors in Islamic teachings?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That Ibn 'Umar heard a man saying: \"No by the Ka'bah\" so Ibn 'Umar said: \"Nothing is sworn by other than Allah, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'Whoever swears by other than Allah, he has committed disbelief or shirk.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1535, Book 20, Hadith 13",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How is disbelief or shirk related to the act of swearing by something other than Allah?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"A Woman vowed to walk to the House of Allah, so the Prophet (ﷺ) asked about that, and he said: 'Verily Allah is in no need of her walking, order her to ride.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1536, Book 20, Hadith 14",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What guidance does Islam provide regarding vows that may cause hardship?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"The Prophet (ﷺ) passed by old man walking (while supported) between his two sons, so he said: 'What is the matter with this one?' They said: \"O Messenger of Allah! He vowed to walk.' He said: 'Verily Allah [the Mighty and Sublime] is in no need of this person punishing himself.'\" He said: \"So he ordered him to ride.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1537, Book 20, Hadith 15",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What guidance does Islam provide regarding fulfilling vows that may cause harm or difficulty?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Do not vow, for the vows does not prevent what is decreed at all, and it only causes the miser to spend (of his wealth).\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1538, Book 20, Hadith 17",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What are the potential consequences of making vows for a person who is naturally miserly?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"I said:'O Messenger of Allah! I had vowed to perform I'tikaf in Al-Masjid Al-Haram for a night during the era of Jahiliyyah.' He said: 'Fulfill your vow.''\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1539, Book 20, Hadith 18",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What is the importance of fulfilling vows in Islam?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"From this father (Ibn Umar) who said: \"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) often would swear with this oath: 'No! By the Changer of the Hearts.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1540, Book 20, Hadith 19",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How does the concept of Allah as the 'Changer of the Hearts' influence a believer's understanding of faith and guidance?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Whoever frees a believing slave, then Allah frees a limb from the Fire for each of his limbs, such that he frees his private parts in lieu of his private parts.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1541, Book 20, Hadith 20",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What are the spiritual benefits mentioned for freeing a slave in Islamic tradition?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"We were seven brothers without a servant except one, and one of us slapped her, so the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered us to free her.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1542, Book 20, Hadith 21",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What actions are recommended in Islam when someone wrongs another person, especially a servant?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam while lying, then he is as he said.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1543, Book 20, Hadith 22",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What is the significance of truthfulness in Islamic teachings?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! My sister vowed that she would walk to the House barefoot and without Khimar (covering).' The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Verily Allah will not do anything with the misery of your sister. She should ride, and cover, and fast three days.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1544, Book 20, Hadith 23",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What alternatives does Islam provide for fulfilling vows that involve hardship?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \"Whoever among you swears, saying in his oath: 'By Al-Lat! By Al-'Uzza!' Then let him say 'La ilaha illa Allah' And whoever says: 'Come let me gamble with you!' Then let him give in charity.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1545, Book 20, Hadith 24",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"How can one rectify the act of inviting someone to gamble according to Islamic teachings?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That Sa'd bin 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about a vow that was due from his mother, who died before fulfilling it. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Fulfill it for her.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1546, Book 20, Hadith 25",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What is the significance of fulfilling vows in Islam, especially for those who have passed away?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man, then it is his salvation from the Fire - each of his limbs suffices for a limb of himself. And any Muslim man that frees two Muslim women, then are his salvation from the Fire - each of their limbs suffices for a limb of himself. And any Muslim woman that frees a Muslim woman, then she is her salvation from the Fire - each of her limb suffices for a limb of herself.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1547, Book 20, Hadith 26",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What are the spiritual benefits for a Muslim man who frees another Muslim man?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"An Army from the armies of the Muslims, whose commander was Salman Al-Farisi, besieged one of the Persian castles. They said: 'O Abu 'Abdullah! Should we charge them?' He said: 'Leave me to call them (to Islam) as I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) call them.' So Salman went to them and said: 'I am only a man from among you, a Persian, and you see that the Arabs obey me. If you become Muslims then you will have the likes of what we have, and from you will be required that which is required from us. If you refuse, and keep your religion, then we will leave you to it, and you will give us the Jizyah from your hands while you are submissive.' He said to them in Persian: 'And you are other than praiseworthy and if you refuse then we will equally resist you.' They said: 'We will not give you the Jizyah, we will fight you instead.' So they said: 'O Abu 'Abdullah! Should we charge them?' He said: 'No.'\" He said: \"So for three days he called them to the same (things), and then he said: 'Charge them.'\" He said: \"So we charged them, and we conquered the castle.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1548, Book 21, Hadith 1",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What options were given to the Persians by Salman Al-Farisi during the siege?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"From his father and he was a Companion who said: \"When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) dispatched any army or battalion, he would say to them: 'If you see a Masjid, or hear someone calling the Adhan, then do not kill anyone.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1549, Book 21, Hadith 2",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What significance does the call to Adhan hold in the context of military engagement according to Islamic teachings?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out for Khaibar, he approached it at night and when he came to a people during the night, he would not attack them until morning. So when the morning came, the Jews came out with their shovels and baskets, then when they saw him, they said: 'Muhammad! By Allah Muhammad has come with the Khamis (an army).' So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Allahu Akbar! Khaibar is destroyed, for whenever we approach the land of people - then what an evil morning for those who have been warned.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1550, Book 21, Hadith 3",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What significance does the phrase 'Allahu Akbar' hold in the context of this event?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"When the Prophet (ﷺ) overtook a people he would stay at the outskirts of their city for three nights.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1551, Book 21, Hadith 4",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What might be the reasons for the Prophet staying at the outskirts of a city for a few days?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) burnt the palm trees of Bani Nadir and cut them down at Al-Buwairah. So Allah revealed: Whatever you cut down of their palm trees, or you left them standing on their trunks, then it was by the permission of Allah, and in the order to disgrace the rebellious.(59:5)\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1552, Book 21, Hadith 5",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What does this event teach about the concept of divine permission in Islamic actions?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"Verily, Allah has honored me over the (other) Prophets\" - or he said: \"My nation over the nations, and He has made the spoils of war lawful for us.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 1553, Book 21, Hadith 6",
