    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"When this Ayah was revealed: 'But you did hide in yourself that which Allah will make manifest... (33:37)' about Zainab bint Jahsh, Zaid had come to the Prophet (ﷺ) complaining, and he wanted to divorce her, so he consulted with the Prophet (ﷺ). The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Keep your wife to yourself, and have Taqwa of Allah (33:37).'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 3212, Book 47, Hadith 264",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What does the interaction between the Prophet (ﷺ) and Zaid teach about seeking counsel in personal matters?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"When this Ayah was revealed about Zainab bint Jahsh: 'So when Zaid had completed his aim with her, We gave her to you in marriage (33:37)' - he said: \"She used to boast to the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ): 'Your families married you (to him) while Allah married me (to him) from above the Seven Heavens.'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 3213, Book 47, Hadith 265",
        "grade":"Sahih(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What does the Quranic revelation regarding Zainab bint Jahsh's marriage indicate about divine intervention in personal matters?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) proposed to me, but I asked him to excuse me. Then Allah [Most High] revealed: 'Verily We have made lawful to you your wives, to whom you have paid their due, and those whom your right hand possess - whom Allah has given to you, and the daughters of your paternal uncles, and the daughters of your paternal aunts, and the daughters of your maternal uncles, and the daughters of your maternal aunts, who migrated with you, and a believing woman if she offers herself to the Prophet... (33:50)' She said: \"So I was not lawful for him because I did not perform Hijrah; I was one of the Tulaqa (those that accepted Islam after the conquest of Makkah).'\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 3214, Book 47, Hadith 266",
        "grade":"Da'if(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"Who were the Tulaqa and what was their significance in early Islamic history?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"All types of women were prohibited for the Messenger of ALlah (ﷺ) except for the believing women among those who emigrated. (Allah) said: 'It is not lawful for you (to marry other) women after this, nor to change them for other wives even though their beauty attracts you, except those whom your right hand possesses (33:52). - And Allah made your believing girls lawful 'And a believing woman if she offers herself to the Prophet (33:50)' and He made every woman of a religion other than Islam unlawful.\" Then He said: \"And whoever disbelieves in faith then fruitless is his work; and in the Hereafter he will be among the losers (5:5).\" And he said: \"Verily We have made lawful to you your wives, to whom you have paid their due, and those whom your right hands possess - whom Allah has given you\" up to His saying: \"A privilege to only you, not for the (rest of) the believers (33:50).\" He made the other types of women unlawful.\"",
        "reference":"Jami` at-Tirmidhi 3215, Book 47, Hadith 267",
        "grade":"Hasan(Darussalam)",
        "question #":"question #3",
        "question":"What privileges were granted specifically to the Prophet Muhammad (ﷺ) concerning marriage?"
    },
    {
        "hadith-eng":"\"The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not die until the women had been made lawful for him.\"",
